{
  "readme": [
    "The per-instance constraints corpus (morph#164). ONE file, TWO readers:",
    "  tests/test_forms_instance_constraints.cpp -- InstanceConstraints::checkValue",
    "  src/qt/forms/tests/tst_DynamicFormInstanceBounds.qml -- a real DynamicForm",
    "",
    "The point of the seam is that ONE declaration both serves a schema and",
    "checks a submitted value, so the two cannot drift. That is only worth",
    "anything if the shipped renderer honours what was served -- otherwise the",
    "instance's range is a second opinion nobody reads, which is the two-keys-",
    "for-one-concept outcome the seam exists to remove.",
    "",
    "'constraints' is the declaration BOTH the served schema and the checked",
    "bound come from: the C++ side rebuilds InstanceConstraints from it and",
    "asserts instanceSchemaJson<ICCapture>() equals 'schemas.decorated' byte for",
    "byte. Regenerate that text from the failure message if the emitter changes.",
    "",
    "The 'compiled' rows are the control: the same values against the",
    "undecorated schemaJson<ICCapture>(), where they are accepted. Without them",
    "a renderer that rejected everything would pass."
  ],
